    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1985855818756215146",
      "url": "https://x.com/DrTonyLeachon/status/1985855818756215146",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/DrTonyLeachon/status/1985855818756215146",
      "text": "🇵🇭 Why We Still Love the Philippines\n\nWe love our country not because it is perfect, but because it is ours.\n\nWe love it despite the corruption that stains our institutions—because the soul of the nation is not found in its politics, but in its people. In the quiet dignity of farmers, the resilience of nurses abroad, the laughter of children playing in flooded streets. We love it because it is home.\n\nWe love it despite the daily bickering, the noise of division on social media—because beneath the clamor lies a shared longing: to be heard, to be healed, to belong. We are a family still learning how to speak truth with grace.\n\nWe love this country even as it is battered by typhoons, earthquakes, and fire—because we have seen it rise again and again. Our land may break, but our spirit does not.\n\nWe love the Philippines because our heroes once did. Because they believed in a future worth dying for. Because we carry their blood, their dreams, their unfinished fight.\n\nPatriotism is not blind loyalty—it is stubborn hope. It is choosing to stay, to speak, to serve, even when it hurts. It is believing that we are still capable of greatness.\n\nWe must not stop.\nWe must step up.\nWho knows—perhaps God and our true heroes are watching, waiting for us to rise.\n\n- Dr. Tony Leachon",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
